; NextDAAD 40-column tilemap mode fixture (2026-08-30).
;
; Compiled and byte-asserted by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run;
; -Txt40 additionally stages it into sd\TXT40\. Drives GFX 0/1 18 (the
; width-select sub-command, src\nextdaad.inc GFX_SUB_TXTMODE, src\
; main.asm tm_width_apply), WINAT/WINSIZE clamping at the live width,
; CENTRE's tmCols-relative window placement, and the $6B save/restore
; across a synchronous video play from 40-col mode.
;
; Verbs:
;   T40   GFX 1 18 - switch to 40-col, clean slate, print at 40
;   T80   GFX 0 18 - switch to 80-col, clean slate, print at 80
;   WINS  WINDOW 1, WINAT 2 2, WINSIZE 10 36, a message that wraps at
;         36 - proves WINAT/WINSIZE clamp and wrap use the live width
;   CENT  WINDOW 2, WINSIZE 3 20, CENTRE - proves CENTRE's tmCols math
;         at whichever width is live when it runs
;   VID   GFX 1 13 - plays video 1 synchronously; from 40-col this
;         exercises the wholesale $6B save/restore carrying the width
;         bit through playback (interrupts.asm's 18-byte restore tail)
;   LEAK  a message ending mid-word, then GFX 1 18 - the pending wrap
;         word must be discarded on switch (main.asm tm_width_apply
;         zeroes wrapLen before windows_init), not leaked onto the
;         cleared screen
;
; V2 header (plain "DRF.exe nextdaad", no -v3) to match every other
; byte-asserted stimulus fixture in this suite.

/CTL
_
/VOC
T40    10  verb
T80    11  verb
WINS   12  verb
CENT   13  verb
VID    14  verb
LEAK   15  verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I don't know that verb - try T40 T80 WINS CENT VID LEAK."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 " "
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "40-col mode#n"
/1 "80-col mode#n"
/2 "This forty column wrap test prints a message long enough that it must break across several lines inside a thirty six column window without losing any words or truncating the text unexpectedly#n"
/3 "CENTRED#n"
/4 "The pending word buffer should not leak this fragment after switching wid"
/5 "NEXTDAAD TXT40 - 40 COLUMN MODE FIXTURE#n"
/6 "back from video, still readable#n"
/7 "VERBS  T40  T80  WINS  CENT  VID  LEAK#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The text mode lab."
/CON
/0
/1
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
; The banner is one-shot (AT 0 closes the gate via GOTO 1), so PROCESS 1
; must be its own UNCONDITIONAL entry - eng_run re-enters PRO 0 after
; every DONE, and a gated PROCESS 1 would never parse again.
> _ _   AT 0
        CLS
        MESSAGE 5
        MESSAGE 7
        GOTO 1
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _     PARSE 0
          REDO
> T40   _ GFX 1 18
          MESSAGE 0
          DONE
> T80   _ GFX 0 18
          MESSAGE 1
          DONE
> WINS  _ WINDOW 1
          WINAT 2 2
          WINSIZE 10 36
          MESSAGE 2
          WINDOW 0
          DONE
> CENT  _ WINDOW 2
          WINSIZE 3 20
          CENTRE
          MESSAGE 3
          WINDOW 0
          DONE
> VID   _ GFX 1 13
          MESSAGE 6
          DONE
> LEAK  _ MESSAGE 4
          GFX 1 18
          DONE
> _ _     NEWTEXT
          SYSMESS 8
          REDO
/END
